{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1369213-jekyll-hyde-a-hypatian-bloodline","id":1369213,"title":"Jekyll-Hyde - A Hypatian Bloodline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-20T15:09:43-08:00","id":1369213,"title":"Jekyll-Hyde - A Hypatian Bloodline","content":"So, I couldn't sleep earlier and decided to spend some time working on a thing that I'd been thinking about ever since I first got a look at Spilled Blood. I figure this is the right place to share it. I don't know how good of a job I did, and lack of sleep might be making it harder for me to notice errors.<br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><b><i>Jekyll-Hyde</i></b></u></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><i>The vampiric condition is defined by the dichotomy between Beast and Man, which struggle for control over their shared soul. Wouldn\u2019t it be better to establish some clear boundaries?</i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">One of the most well-known and populous Hypatian bloodlines, the Jekyll-Hydes are the vampiric legacy of \u2018The Strange Case of Dr. Jekyll and Mr. Hyde\u2019, a famous novel that tells the story of a doctor who brews a strange elixir that brings out his inner beast and lets him indulge his repressed urges free from guilt as the mysterious Mr. Hyde. Very few Dyads believe the book to be a record of true events, but most assume their bloodline\u2019s mysterious founders either inspired the story or were themselves inspired by it.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The Jekyll-Hydes are the duality of the vampiric condition made manifest, two-faced beings that walk a tightrope between man and beast. Some of them struggle with their condition, while others embrace it wholeheartedly, but most are fairly divided on it, fittingly enough. They have a reputation for being either the best or worst kind of vampire, depending upon which part of their self happens to be dominant at the time, but in dealing with their kind one would be wise to remember that the Man is just as capable of evil as the Beast.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Background:</b> The Jekyll-Hydes began in the early eighteen-nineties, when a strange alchemical formula began circulating throughout the Hypatian community, purporting to be the work of \u2018Henry Jekyll and Edward Hyde\u2019. Most of them assumed it to be some kind of joke or saw the names as aliases, but nonetheless some of them attempted to brew the mysterious elixir that the formula described. Those who drank the potion found that they now had their own Mr. Hyde, that their psyches had been split in two in a manner much more observable than before. The early Dyads called themselves the \u2018Jani\u2019, after the ancient two-faced god of boundaries, but the name \u2018Jekyll-Hyde\u2019 proved to be more enduring and popular.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>The Becoming:</b> Like their parent clan, the Jekyll-Hydes are incapable of the Embrace, though it is possible for a Blight to \u2018naturally\u2019 join the bloodline if the donor of the Vitae used to brew their dose of Hypatia\u2019s vampiric elixir was a Dyad, or if one mixes the that potion with the one used to join the bloodline proper. The majority of Jekyll-Hydes were inducted by an Avus, but the method by which the earliest members of the bloodline inducted themselves is still possible; the elixir requires three dots of the Blood Chymistry Merit to create and is brewed over the course of a single night from a mixture of calcium chloride, cerebrospinal fluid, citric acid, ether, phosphorous and Vitae.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Most Dyads prioritise Mental or Social Attributes in their Jekyll-Forms, usually interacting with others primarily with this form, as their high effective Humanity rating means that they don\u2019t have to worry so much about their clan bane. Most Hyde-Forms are Physical or Mentally focused, though many of them maintain a high Composure. Many Jani study Blood Chymistry, but there are a fair number who don\u2019t, or do so only in one form and not the other.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>In the Danse Macabre:</b> Most Jekyll-Hydes in the Covenants associate themselves with the Ordo Dracul, but a considerable number have found a place for themselves in the First Estate. A few of them work with the Carthian Movement, while others worship Janus in the Circle of the Crone, but it doesn\u2019t seem like any of their number get along well with the Lancea et Sanctum.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">-o-o-o-</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Nickname:</b> Dyads, Jani</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Clan:</b> Hypatians</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Bloodline Bane (The Curse of Duality):</b> Like their namesake, the Jekyll-Hydes are each drawn between two different identities, which loosely correspond to the Beast and the Man. The Dyad rolls a dicepool equal to her Humanity whenever she awakens from daysleep or torpor, success means she will remain in her \u2018Jekyll-Form\u2019 until the next time she wakes, while failure means she assumes her \u2018Hyde-Form\u2019. A Jani also rolls to determine which form she will take when she drinks the same concoction that allows a Hypatian to join the bloodline without an Avus, though doing this either adds two dice or removes two dice, whichever she prefers.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The Jekyll-Form is considered to be Humanity 10, regardless of the vampire\u2019s actual Humanity rating, for all purposes except determining the length of torpor and the roll that determines which form she will take upon waking from slumber. In this form, she is incapable of frenzy. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Like the other form, the Hyde-Form is considered to be Humanity 1, regardless of the vampire\u2019s actual Humanity rating, for all purposes except determining the length of torpor and the roll that determines which form she will take upon waking from slumber. In this form, she is incapable of resisting frenzy, though she may still ride the wave.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Jekyll-Hyde with Humanity 0 are permanently stuck in the Hyde-Form and do not benefit from the Hyde-Form\u2019s usual effective Humanity rating.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Bloodline Disciplines:</b> Auspex, Celerity, Nightmare, Resilience</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Favoured Attributes:</b> Composure or Wits</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">-o-o-o-</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><i>Two Faced</i></b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The Dyads are divided between two identities and two forms, which appear markedly different from each other. Some Jekyll-Hydes\u2019 two forms appear similar enough as to seem related, while others look like entirely unrelated people, to the point that they might seem to be radically different age or the opposite sex. The difference between the two forms is more than just one of appearance and Humanity, however, as even a Dyad whose forms look near to identical will usually display radically different aptitudes in each form.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">A Jekyll-Hyde\u2019s two forms are built as two distinct characters with the exact same total amount of experience, though they will typically spend it differently, when one of them gains experience so does the other. They might have very different Aspirations, Attributes, Devotions, Disciplines, Skills and Merits, though if the latter represents something that they share with their other form, than that form must also buy that Merit. In addition, the two forms always have the same Blood Potency and Humanity, so both forms need to spend experience to raise these two particular things. Finally, the two forms typically either have the same Dirge and Mask, or invert them, but this isn\u2019t always the case.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T00:20:34-08:00","id":1369293,"title":"","content":"As the writer who came up with the Hypatians, I'm really happy to see this kind of fan work!<br /> <br /> A few thoughts:<br /> <br /> -- I really like the concept (suits the clan well), but I think the weakness/benefit is a bit too strong on both ends. Instead, maybe try making it a standing bonus or penalty on effective Humanity depending on what form they take.<br /> -- This isn't a hard rule, but typically bloodlines still have one Favored Attribute from their parent clan.<br /> -- The dual character sheets idea might be too much bookkeeping, but the idea is cool. Maybe rather than a whole separate sheet, the two forms redistribute certain trait dots, up to and including Discipline dots. Maybe you could tie it to Blood Potency (the stronger you are, the more variable your forms).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T02:11:18-08:00","id":1369309,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback!<br /> <br /> 1. Yeah, I was thinking that as well. Maybe a +3 Bonus or -3 Penalty? Do you think the Frenzy-thing is a good idea?<br /> 2. Oh, I didn't notice that, but I'll fix it at some point. Truth be told, I wasn't even sure whether seperate Favoured Attributes would make sense for them.<br /> 3. Yeah, I was concerned it might be a bit too much bookkeeping. This idea is probably better to be honest, rather than the separate sheets. I don't know how I'd go about tying it to Blood Potency, though. Maybe I should just limit it to Attributes and Disciplines?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-21T08:33:48-08:00","id":1369380,"title":"","content":"Brainstorming: this is a really neat idea though I'd water it down for the sake of bookkeeping and sanity. Maybe change the favored attributes: Composure for Jekyll, Resolve for Hyde, and this dot moves around depending on which form they roll into. Force them to have inverted Dirge and Mask. When in Jekyll form, they get +2 dice to Resist Frenzy. When in the Hyde form, they cannot Resist Frenzy, though they may Ride the Wave (failure results in a dramatic frenzy as usual). This preserves the theme of &quot;Jekyll is your character, and Hyde is his dark side that does his dirty work.&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe if they fail a Frenzy roll as Jekyll they automatically switch over to Hyde?<br /> <br /> If you want shapeshifting or dot swapping to be part of the concept, maybe Protean as in-clan discipline with some special Devotions for that purpose?<br /> <br /> I'll keep thinking. You've built a really fun concept.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> Maybe something like:<br /> <br /> New Devotion: Lanyon's Demise (Protean 2, Nightmare 2):<br /> Cost: At least 1 Vitae<br /> Action: Instant<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> For each Vitae spent, the Dyad may re-allocate one dot of his Finesse or Resistance attributes to a Power Attribute. The re-allocation does not need to be within the same category.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":12157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","user":"Kvark","date":". 02-21-2020, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}